# Hotspots: what Story.use(spot) plays (cue use.<spot>, or use._default). The spots are SPOT_<id> markers in the
# level, or entries in data/world.json "spots". Ported from v1, with every line put in Mano's own
# head (V2-10): `think` (first person, his pen); only stage sounds (*clunk*) stay on the narrator.
# A cue made only of thoughts (no choice, no minigame) plays as barks: Mano keeps walking while it shows
# (DialogueData.is_think_only, main.interact). The old v1 texts are in tests/fixtures/v1_rewrites.json.

~ use.velib
if night()
	think: The bike rack under the street lamp. Still every tyre flat. Loyal.
else
	think: A bike rack. Every bike on it has a flat tyre. Consistent, at least.

~ use.logo
think: EPITA. École pour l'informatique et les techniques avancées.
think: Also: my second home, apparently. [if not night()]
think: At night it's just home. Don't tell my parents. [if night()]

~ use.elevator
think: EN PANNE. The sticker is so old it has its own sticker.

~ use.north_door
think: The rue Voltaire doors, and right behind them the périphérique. Not today.

~ use.rules
think: "No food in the computer rooms. Sealed water bottles only."
think: Someone has drawn a sad croissant. I feel seen.

~ use.slide
think: Algorithmique - plus courts chemins. "QCM vendredi 9h".
think: Tomorrow, 9:00. I did not read that email. [if not night()]
think: The projector's off, the slide burnt in. Tomorrow, 9:00. Still true. [if night()]

~ use.gate
if clock_after("18:00")
	think: The gate to rue Roger Salengro. Locked since 18:00, on the dot.
else
	think: The gate to rue Roger Salengro. Locked after 18:00, so: soon.

~ use.vending
if night()
	think: The vending machine hums in the dark. Still 1.50 euros. Still no.
else
	think: Chips: 1.50 euros for 30 grams. My wallet says no.

~ use.stickers
think: A column covered in stickers: LSE, ACU, GCC, a cat...
think: ...and one that just says "SEGV". Same. [if not night()]
think: ...and "SEGV", glowing a bit under the party lights. Still same. [if night()]

~ use.coffee
if coffee_given and chapter == 2 and not spare_coffee and not sup_awake
	think: The machine hums. It owes me one.
	- Press the button anyway
		$ sfx machine_clunk
		nar: *clunk*
		think: A free coffee. Guilt, probably. For someone who needs it more.
		$ set spare_coffee
		$ toast "A spare coffee" coffee
	- Leave it
		think: Some debts are better left unpaid.
elif spare_coffee
	think: One coffee in my hand already. Someone in Amphi 4 needs it more.
elif coffee or coffee_given
	think: The coffee machine hums. Smugly.
elif paid
	think: My 2 euros are still stuck inside. Time to shake it again.
	$ minigame coffee win=c2.coffee_ok lose=c2.coffee_fail
elif coins < 2
	think: COFFEE: 2 euros, and I have {{coins}}. The machine judges me silently.
else
	think: COFFEE: 2 euros. Buy one?
	- Buy (2 euros)
		$ add coins -2
		$ set paid = true
		$ sfx coin
		nar: *clunk*
		think: ...nothing comes out. The machine is stuck!
		$ minigame coffee win=c2.coffee_ok lose=c2.coffee_fail
	- No
		mano: My wallet says no.

~ use.sign
if sign
	think: "BACK IN 5 MIN." Still. Since 9:00.
else
	think: A sticky note on the desk: "BACK IN 5 MIN." It is dated 9:00.
	think: That was over nine hours ago. Long five minutes.
	$ set sign = true
	$ clue "Mme Dupont has been \"back in 5 min\" since 9:00. Probably in the cafeteria, in the X building, on cour Pasteur."

~ use.lostbox
if lf_twist
	think: Five strangers' AirPods and one empty slot. The empty one's mine.
else
	think: LOST & FOUND, locked. Only Mme Dupont has the key.

~ use.coin_planter
if got_planter
	think: Just soil and a birch leaf.
else
	think: Something shiny in the Gally crate... 1 euro! A bit muddy, still counts.
	$ coin planter

~ use.coin_sofa
if got_sofa
	think: Only crumbs left. The chip is staring at me.
else
	think: Between the sofa cushions... 1 euro! And a fossilised chip.
	think: I keep the euro. The chip keeps the sofa.
	$ coin sofa

~ use._default
think: ...

# The side story "Segmentation fault" (side.dlg): the BDE's babyfoot air horn on the bar, chapter 2 (world.json spot horn)
~ use.horn
think: The BDE's babyfoot air horn, left on the bar. "For goals only."
think: Waking a SUP before his soutenance is a goal.
$ set horn
$ toast "An air horn" babyfoot
